      "writtenOn": "2025-07-24T17:44:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To match libwebp style, there are other comments that can be made in nallocinc.h. We can treat that as contributed code and leave it as is. I would also like a way to disable nalloc; have a build flag to enable it would be best (`WEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC` or so)",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f32f0775_e13d6051",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4230816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T18:39:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok for build time, did you mean something at runtime ? NALLOC_FREQ can already be used to have more or less allocations failures",
      "parentUuid": "f78c881e_39d9aaea",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "386bb9dc_067f0ebf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T22:58:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Ok for build time, did you mean something at runtime ? NALLOC_FREQ can already be used to have more or less allocations failures\n\nIf the default for `NALLOC_FREQ` when the environment variable is undefined means no allocations will fail then this should be OK.",
      "parentUuid": "f32f0775_e13d6051",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f6da1b6_49e56681",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4230816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T18:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, now the default build (without WEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC) does not make any allocations fail\n\nBut, I still would like to have oss-fuzz run with allocations failing\n\nSo, the default runtime, if build was with WEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC, is to make allocations fail...\n\nI am adding a new randomization feature : one run out of 2 will not have allocations failure, while the other out of 2 will fail at a random frequency between 1/32 and 1/2^20",
      "parentUuid": "386bb9dc_067f0ebf",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d807a70_e756c68b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-30T22:36:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Well, now the default build (without WEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC) does not make any allocations fail\n\u003e \n\u003e But, I still would like to have oss-fuzz run with allocations failing\n\u003e \n\u003e So, the default runtime, if build was with WEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC, is to make allocations fail...\n\u003e \n\u003e I am adding a new randomization feature : one run out of 2 will not have allocations failure, while the other out of 2 will fail at a random frequency between 1/32 and 1/2^20\n\nThis sounds reasonable, though decreasing the low end might find some (less likely to occur) bugs. I think it makes sense to be able to allow normal fuzzing to occur without allocation failures. If that\u0027s possible with the same binary then great. I don\u0027t see that happening in the current patchset, though. With none of the environment variables defined the nalloc code should be a noop, correct?",
      "parentUuid": "0f6da1b6_49e56681",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "395a8eab_500f0262",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4230816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-31T10:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e decreasing the low end might find some (less likely to occur) bugs\n\nWhich number do you want to decrease ? 1/32 ? 1/2^20 ?\n\n\u003e I think it makes sense to be able to allow normal fuzzing to occur without allocation failures.\n\nThat is possible and default build if you do not build with DWEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC\n\n\u003e If that\u0027s possible with the same binary then great\n\nI am adding that possibility. If you built with DWEBP_FUZZER_ENABLE_NALLOC, but want to run without allocations failures, you can use env variable `NALLOC_FREQ\u003d0`\n\n\u003e With none of the environment variables defined the nalloc code should be a noop, correct?\n\nI do not agree as I want allocations to fail on ossfuzz, and ossfuzz will not define NALLOC_FREQ or such...\nIs the solution `NALLOC_FREQ\u003d0` good enough for you ?",
      "parentUuid": "7d807a70_e756c68b",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67fd0e36_70ddaf29",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
