      "author": {
        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-31T22:04:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e NALLOC_FREQ\u003d0 and a default of 0\n\u003e \n\u003e But then, oss-fuzz will not run with allocations failures\n\u003e \n\u003e Do you see a way to achieve that ?\n\nThe Dockerfile can have an `ENV` entry added:\n\nhttps://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/blob/master/projects/git/Dockerfile#L37",
      "parentUuid": "b3042194_296874e7",
      "revId": "8ff771147d21fe68d10b9524022073c67f6eec1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
